WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
A hairdryer roars at
two thousand watts,

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.410
but only for five minutes a day.

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.870
A tiny ten-watt L E
D bulb glows quietly,

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.630
left on all day and all night.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.690
One is two hundred
times more powerful.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.770
The other never stops.

7
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.950
So which one transfers
more energy each day?

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.050
In this mission, you'll find
out what the power rating on an

9
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.510
appliance really means.

10
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.930
You'll calculate electrical
power from current and potential

11
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.850
difference, and see how power
and time together decide the

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.550
energy transferred.

13
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.180
Your mission: find out which one
transfers more energy each day.
